WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:07.600
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I am going to&nbsp;
explain an American supernatural horror film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:15.920
called “Carrie”. Spoilers ahead!&nbsp;
Watch out and take care!
&nbsp;

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:22.640
Margaret White is a deluded religious fanatic&nbsp;
who thinks everything is sinful, especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:28.720
if it is related to women, their bodies, and sex.&nbsp;
In the opening scene, she is on her bloodied bed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:34.640
screaming in pain and asking God to forgive her&nbsp;
sins. She is so unmindful of the real world that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:41.120
she thinks she is dying of cancer when in reality,&nbsp;
she is in labor. When the pain finally subsides,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:46.640
she looks in between her legs and freezes&nbsp;
in shock to see a newborn girl. Margaret&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:50.960
thinks that the infant is the result of the&nbsp;
sin she committed with her former husband.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:56.240
She brings out a pair of scissors, getting ready&nbsp;
to murder the baby but cannot bring herself to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:01.600
it. The little girl is later named Carrie. Over&nbsp;
the years, Margaret forces her religious beliefs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:06.800
on Carrie and doesn’t give her any freedom&nbsp;
at all. She refrains her from making friends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:12.480
talking to men, and doesn’t let her go to school&nbsp;
for most of her life. When Carrie turns sixteen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:17.280
children's rights activists forcefully make&nbsp;
Margaret let her daughter go to high school.
&nbsp;

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:23.280
However, because of her antisocial and introverted&nbsp;
nature, Carrie is always made fun of. She never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:28.880
talks to anyone and stares in shock when girls&nbsp;
show cleavage or couples kiss. The concept of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:33.360
dating is foreign to her. One day, while&nbsp;
the students are playing water volleyball,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:39.040
Carrie accidentally hits the popular girl Sue&nbsp;
in the head. Sue's friend, Chris, makes fun of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:44.080
Carrie and everyone laughs at her. After the&nbsp;
class, they go to the shower room to change.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:49.440
Carrie gets her first period while showering and&nbsp;
starts to panic. She has never been taught about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:54.720
periods or anything that has to do with female&nbsp;
anatomy. The blood running down her legs makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.720 --> 00:02:00.080
her think she is dying of an illness. She runs&nbsp;
around, frantically asking the girls for help. 
&nbsp;

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:05.120
Chris realizes that Carrie doesn't understand&nbsp;
what menstruation is and makes fun of her. Soon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:10.640
all other girls join and throw tampons at&nbsp;
her while filming her crying. Sue feels bad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:16.160
for Carrie but doesn't stop the girls, scared to&nbsp;
be declared an outcast like her. They only stop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:21.280
when the gym teacher, Ms. Desjardin arrives&nbsp;
there. Carrie starts having a panic attack,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:26.960
screaming and crying even after the girls stop. To&nbsp;
calm her down, the teacher slaps her in the face.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:32.880
As the girls walk away, Carrie stares at the light&nbsp;
bulb in anger and it coincidentally shatters. When&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:37.440
the principal is informed of the incident, he&nbsp;
asks Ms. Desjardin to punish the bullies as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:42.400
she wishes. He also tells Carrie to calm down&nbsp;
because they have called her mother. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:46.640
the thought of her mother finding out she&nbsp;
got her periods makes her even more nervous.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:51.520
She hyperventilates and a water cooler&nbsp;
in the room shatters mysteriously. 
&nbsp;

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:56.320
Sometime later, Margaret comes to pick her&nbsp;
daughter and sees Chris and her boyfriend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.320 --> 00:03:01.200
fmaking out. She doesn’t want such influence&nbsp;
around her daughter and prays to God to show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:06.880
the “spoiled” kids the correct path to life.&nbsp;
On the way home, Carrie asks Margaret why she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:11.920
never taught her about menstruation but Margaret&nbsp;
doesn’t answer. Before getting out of the car,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:17.360
a neighbor kid calls Carrie a weirdo. She looks&nbsp;
at him and makes him fall off his bike. Similar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:21.920
strange things have been happening to her for&nbsp;
the past few months and she doesn’t know why. 
&nbsp;

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:26.880
Inside the house, Margaret is banging her head&nbsp;
against the wall, apologizing to God for creating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:32.160
her daughter who will someday sin as she sinned&nbsp;
with her former husband. She even creates fake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:38.400
bible verses to make Carrie believe that bleeding&nbsp;
on a period is a sin and she has become a sinner.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:42.480
Carrie knows that her mother is lying because&nbsp;
Ms. Desjardin explained everything about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:47.680
menstruation earlier. She retaliates that it&nbsp;
is normal and every girl gets it. This makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:52.640
Margaret knock her in the head with a bible.&nbsp;
She locks her inside a tiny “praying closet”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:57.920
asking her to come out only when she has asked&nbsp;
for forgiveness from God. Carrie yells in anger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:03.360
which makes the door crack. She then lays eyes&nbsp;
on a sculpture of Jesus that starts to bleed. 
&nbsp;

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:10.320
Somewhere else, Sue and her boyfriend Tommy are&nbsp;
in Tommy’s jeep. At his request, they make love&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:15.440
in the car. After getting dressed, Sue tells him&nbsp;
that she feels guilty for not helping Carrie in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:20.800
the shower room. Meanwhile, Chris is with her&nbsp;
boyfriend Billy at her house. Unlike Sue, she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:25.920
shows no regret whatsoever, even though she was&nbsp;
the one who initiated the bullying. To humiliate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:30.800
Carrie even more, she uploads the video of the&nbsp;
incident on the internet. Back in the house,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:35.680
Margaret is calmly sewing clothes while singing&nbsp;
songs. It is almost as if she has forgotten&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:39.760
about what happened with her daughter earlier.&nbsp;
She eventually lets Carrie out of the closet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:44.960
after confirming that she prayed to god. 
The next day at school, Ms. Desjardin gathers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:49.680
Chris, Sue, along with all the other girls who&nbsp;
were involved. As a punishment, they will have to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:56.080
do suicide sprints for an hour for the rest of the&nbsp;
week. Anyone who disobeys will be denied access&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.080 --> 00:05:01.600
to the upcoming prom. Chris calls the punishment&nbsp;
bullshit and challenges Ms. Desjardin to make her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:07.680
stop from coming to prom. An enraged Ms. Desjardin&nbsp;
suspends her and revokes her prom privileges.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:12.560
Chris protests and tries to rally the other&nbsp;
girls to join her but no one supports her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:16.560
not even her best friend Sue.  
In the meantime, the entire school has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:20.880
watched the video of Carrie getting bullied.&nbsp;
They make fun of her and even go as far as to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:29.760
spray graffiti on her locker that says, 'Carrie&nbsp;
White eats shit'. Humiliated and filled with rage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:34.640
she goes to the bathroom and concentrates on&nbsp;
the mirror which shatters because of her stare.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:40.000
Carrie finally begins to realize she has the&nbsp;
power of psychokinesis, which means she can move&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:45.200
objects and people using only her mind.
To learn more about her power, she goes to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:49.760
the library and reads several books about&nbsp;
psychokinesis. The report on it makes her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:55.680
believe that like menstruation, having such power&nbsp;
is also normal for some people. In the next class,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:59.440
she is called to the front of the&nbsp;
classroom to read a poem. When she is done,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:04.720
Sue’s boyfriend Tommy mutters an insult under&nbsp;
his breath, but when asked to speak louder, he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:10.240
claims that Carrie’s poem was awesome. Carrie is&nbsp;
shocked and shy that a guy complimented her. 
&nbsp;

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:14.960
Meanwhile, Chris calls her lawyer father to&nbsp;
the school to try and overturn her revoked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:20.320
prom privileges. She plays the victim accusing&nbsp;
Ms. Desjardin of verbally abusing her. To prove&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:24.960
her wrong, Ms. Desjardin asks for her phone&nbsp;
that has the video of her bullying Carrie.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:29.120
However, Chris refuses to hand it,&nbsp;
proving that she is guilty. 
&nbsp;

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:34.720
At night, Carrie tests her power by levitating&nbsp;
books and her bed. Margaret hears a noise and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:39.840
comes upstairs with a knife to investigate.&nbsp;
By then, Carrie is pretending to sleep so she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:46.320
puts the knife down. The next day, Sue asks her&nbsp;
boyfriend Tommy to take Carrie to the prom. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:51.360
believes that Carrie deserves one night of fun&nbsp;
and is ready to miss out on senior prom for her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:57.840
Tommy wants to go with Sue but on being insisted&nbsp;
repeatedly, he agrees. Then, he walks up to Carrie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:03.040
and asks her out to prom. A surprised Carrie&nbsp;
thinks he is pranking her and runs away. 
&nbsp;

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:07.680
Later, Ms. Desjardin finds her crying in&nbsp;
the locker room. When asked what is wrong,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:12.000
Carrie tells her about Tommy’s proposal. The&nbsp;
teacher supports Carrie but she also knows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:17.280
that Tommy thinks of her as an outcast. She&nbsp;
finds Sue and Tommy and warns them to rethink&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:22.160
if they are planning to humiliate Carrie. 
After school, Tommy drives to Carrie's house,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:27.040
much to her horror because she doesn’t want her&nbsp;
mother to know she talks to boys. He declares that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:32.560
he will only leave if she agrees to go to prom&nbsp;
with him. Carrie says yes but under the condition&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:38.240
that he will bring her home by 10:30 pm. She is&nbsp;
excited to finally be like the rest of the kids.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:43.200
To prepare for prom, she goes shopping but none&nbsp;
of the dresses are under her budget. So instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:48.720
she buys fabric to sew one herself. Chris&nbsp;
sees Carrie shopping and is filled with rage.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:53.120
She, along with her friends, plan&nbsp;
to play a prank on her at prom. 
&nbsp;

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:58.320
On returning home, Carrie sees an angry Margaret&nbsp;
waiting for her. She tells her mother that she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:03.200
is going to prom but Margaret declares she&nbsp;
won’t allow her. Carrie grows frustrated and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:08.480
levitates things to release her anger. Margaret&nbsp;
prays to god, assuming that the devil has taken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:13.440
over her daughter. Carrie asks her to stop&nbsp;
talking but Margaret prays even louder.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:18.800
Eventually, she makes her mother levitate, making&nbsp;
her go quiet. She releases her a while later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:23.840
declaring that the conversation is over. 
Meanwhile, Chris and Billy are at a farm with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:28.800
their group of friends. They collect blood by&nbsp;
slitting a pig’s throat. Then, they break into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:34.400
the gymnasium which is also the prom venue. They&nbsp;
rig the pail with the pig blood, intending to dump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:40.080
it on Carrie when she is on stage. On the prom&nbsp;
night, Carrie gets ready and applies light makeup.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:45.120
She looks stunning but is very nervous.
Margaret asks her to dress modestly but Carrie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:48.480
doesn’t bother arguing with her. Margaret&nbsp;
tells her daughter that everyone is going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:53.440
to laugh at her which makes Carrie more nervous&nbsp;
than she already is. She locks her mother in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:58.560
praying closet before making her way out. Tommy&nbsp;
is speechless when he sees her. They go to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:04.320
prom hand in hand and Tommy introduces her to his&nbsp;
friends. Ms. Desjardin also compliments her dress&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:09.920
and asks her to have fun. With time, she loosens&nbsp;
up and feels much more comfortable around Tommy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:14.880
A while later, the two slow dance together. 
The night cannot get any better for Carrie but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:20.080
then, Billy and Chris break into the venue. They&nbsp;
wait under the temporary stage to execute their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:26.080
plan. They have rigged the Prom King and Queen&nbsp;
election to ensure Carrie and Tommy are elected.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:28.960
When the couple climbs to the&nbsp;
stage to receive the awards,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:34.720
they will drop the bucket of blood on her. 
Before the election, Chris sends Sue a text&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:40.400
that says they are about to humiliate Carrie. A&nbsp;
horrified Sue races to the prom to stop her. 
&nbsp;

00:09:40.400 --> 00:09:45.120
Soon, Tommy and Carrie win the titles of Prom&nbsp;
king and queen. They are called to the stage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:50.080
as everyone applauds for them. Sue also gets&nbsp;
to the building and sees Chris in the rafters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:55.440
seconds away from dumping the blood on Carrie.&nbsp;
Ms. Desjardin sees Sue and thinks she is here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.440 --> 00:10:01.920
to ruin the moment. So, she locks inside a room&nbsp;
without listening to what she has to say. At last,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:07.520
Chris pulls the rope, dumping the blood on&nbsp;
Carrie. She also hacks the monitor and plays&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:12.640
the video from the day she got her period. 
Everyone laughs as Ms. Desjardin comes forward&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:18.480
to help her. But by now, Carrie has lost&nbsp;
rationality. She pushes Ms. Desjardin back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:24.400
without touching her and everyone gasps. Seconds&nbsp;
later, the pail falls on Tommy’s head, killing him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:29.680
instantly. Carrie loses control of her power and&nbsp;
pushes the crowd away with a single scream. 
&nbsp;

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:34.640
Chris and Billy manage to escape and get in their&nbsp;
car. However, when the others try to run outside,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:39.440
Carrie locks all the doors and windows. 
Next, she throws the tables and chairs at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:45.040
crowd, killing them one by one. She also holds&nbsp;
some girls to the ground so they are killed after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:50.160
being trampled. The place lights on fire when&nbsp;
she breaks the stage lights and electrical wires.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:56.480
She puts Ms. Desjardin safely on the stage and&nbsp;
finishes off the rest of the crowd. She then flies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.480 --> 00:11:02.480
outside looking for Billy and Chris. They drive&nbsp;
away in their car but are chased behind. Billy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:06.800
tries to run her over but Carrie stops the&nbsp;
car with her power, causing him to hit his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.800 --> 00:11:12.560
head and die instantly. Chris tries to run over&nbsp;
her again but Carrie launches the vehicle into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:17.600
a gas station. She then watches as Chris&nbsp;
dies slowly, stuck to the windshield.  
&nbsp;

00:11:17.600 --> 00:11:22.080
Following that, she goes home and notices&nbsp;
her mother isn’t in the praying closet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:27.040
She bathes to clean off all the blood. Margaret&nbsp;
finally appears in front of her and Carrie hugs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:32.000
her mother, claiming that she was right about&nbsp;
everyone making fun of her. Margaret thinks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:37.200
that she is being punished for sinning with her&nbsp;
husband and stabs Carrie with a butcher knife. 
&nbsp;

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:41.840
Carrie tries to save herself but Margaret goes&nbsp;
into a frenzy and chases her into the kitchen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.400 --> 00:11:47.760
She pins Carrie down and is about to stab her&nbsp;
again when Carrie uses her power to stop her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:54.080
She sends several sharp objects towards Margaret,&nbsp;
crucifying her. Then, she cries holding her dying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.080 --> 00:12:00.560
mother and regretting what she did. At last, she&nbsp;
uses her power to destroy the house. Just then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.560 --> 00:12:05.280
Sue arrives at the house and tries to stop&nbsp;
Carrie. She is about to kill her as well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:11.680
but halts after realizing Sue is pregnant.&nbsp;
Carrie smiles and claims that it is a girl.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.680 --> 00:12:16.720
She sends Sue outside to save her from the&nbsp;
falling ceiling. Moments later, Margaret&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:16.720 --> 00:12:22.160
and Carrie die under the collapsing house. 
Some months later, Sue is in a hospital bed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:28.000
screaming in pain while giving birth. Suddenly,&nbsp;
a bloodied hand emerges from her and she wakes up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:33.120
realizing it is just a dream. Her mother comforts&nbsp;
her as she hyperventilates, thinking that she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:38.160
is about to give birth to Carrie. 
